{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218671,"nonce":"kRl5rMBUtqEnVBmuWFNBbXiG8e4=","title":"__zyntax_effect_lookup_op indexes the op table with no bounds check","message":"`(frame.op_table as *const *mut u8).add(op_index)` reads whatever\nfollows the table if op_index is out of range and returns it as a\nfunction pointer. With op-table slots now kept aligned the index should\nnever exceed the table, but nothing enforces it. Defence in depth needs\nthe table length in HandlerFrame, which changes the arity of\n__zyntax_effect_push_handler; compiled code calls it and an ABI test\npins the arity at 4. Do it if this class recurs; not worth the ABI\nchurn on speculation.","files":null}]}